# MixAuto turn-by-turn navigation

## Agent front matter

**Owners:** `NavigationRouteFetcher.kt`, `ConventionalRouteSelector.kt`, `RouteRenderer.kt` (route line / greying only), `data/navigation/NavigationVoiceController.kt`, step/reroute logic in `MapLibreEngineImpl` / `LocationTrackingController`.

**Common tasks:** off-route reroute (35 m, 4 confirms), conventional OSRM pick (`alternatives=3`), in-nav lighter-traffic alternate (TomTom grey line + chip), nav TTS phrases.

**Anti-patterns:** route picker UI (removed — auto-picks conventional); using `RouteRenderer` changes to fix puck smoothness; reroute without `radiuses=25;unlimited` + bearings on parallel streets.

## Routing / off-route / reroute

- `router.project-osrm.org` returns 403 for third-party apps — use `routing.openstreetmap.de/routed-car` in `NavigationRouteFetcher`; set `User-Agent: MixAutoCarLauncher/1.0` on OSRM requests (same as Nominatim)
- Turn-by-turn navigation: `fullRouteSteps` / `currentStepIndex` in `MapLibreEngineImpl`; `evaluateStepAdvancement()` runs on GPS fixes when `isNavigating` — do not overwrite `streetName` with "Current location" during navigation
- Step advance threshold 25 m; arrival at 15 m from destination or when step index exhausts; `navigationArrivalTriggered` prevents duplicate arrival coroutines
- Off-route reroute: `routeGeometryPoints` + `checkOffRoute()` in `evaluateStepAdvancement()` — **35 m** threshold (urban parallel streets), **4** consecutive off-route fixes (`REROUTE_CONFIRM_COUNT = 4`), **20 s** cooldown, **8 s** post-maneuver grace (`offRouteGraceUntilMs`); reroute TTS deduped to once per **30 s** in `NavigationVoiceController`; `startNavigation(..., isReroute=true)` skips `showRouteThenDive()` and calls `enterNavigationCamera()` directly
- Reroute (`isReroute=true`) uses `fetchOsrmRoutesWithAlternatives` + `ConventionalRouteSelector` with OSRM `radiuses=25;unlimited` + optional origin `bearings` so the new route starts on the road the driver is actually on (avoids snapping back onto a close parallel original); unconstrained OSRM fallback if the tight radius returns no route; no route picker / TomTom lighter-traffic alternate on reroute
- Road-snap during nav: engage ≤ **18 m** / release **22 m** — do not snap across parallel streets; `updateRouteProgress()` uses **raw** GPS and **freezes** greying while `distToRoute > 25 m`; when the puck rejoins (`≤ 18 m`), force-sync the traveled/remaining split (forward catch-up or on-route backtrack) so a stuck cyan line unsticks

## Conventional OSRM routing

- Initial navigate fetches OSRM `alternatives=3` + parallel `TomTomRoutingClient.fetchRoute()` when `tomTomApiKey` set
- `ConventionalRouteSelector` scores routes (turn density, short unnamed steps, left turns); picks lowest score within **+12% duration** vs fastest OSRM option
- Always applies conventional route → `showRouteThenDive()` — **no route picker**
- Fallback when OSRM empty: TomTom-only route via `tomTomToRouteResult()`
- Unit tests: `ConventionalRouteSelectorTest.kt`

## In-nav lighter-traffic alternate

- When TomTom returns a geometrically distinct route that is ≥**60 s** faster than conventional **or** has `trafficDelaySeconds ≤ 60` and shorter ETA, show grey line (`ROUTE_LIGHTER_TRAFFIC_*` in `RouteRenderer`) + **"Lighter traffic"** chip in `CarMapViewContainer`
- Tap grey line (`ROUTE_TOMTOM_LAYER_ID` hit test in `handleMapPointSelection`) or chip → `switchToLighterTrafficAlternate()` applies TomTom route immediately (no confirm dialog, no second overview)
- Cleared on free-drive, arrival, switch, reroute start
- Requires TomTom Routing API on key (non-fatal omit when fetch fails)

## Voice guidance (TTS)

- Navigation TTS: `NavigationVoiceController` in `data/navigation/` — owned by **`MapHostViewModel`**, passed to `MapLibreEngineImpl`; hooks from `activateNavigationTracking()` (`onNavigationDrivingStarted`), `evaluateStepAdvancement()` (`onNavTick`/`onStepAdvanced`), reroute/arrival/`startFreeDrive`; silent during route overview and `navigationCameraTransitionActive`
- Nav voice phrases (Option A street-first): per maneuver — **early** at `timeToTurn ≤ 35 s` (`buildAheadCue`: *"Ahead, turn left onto {street}."*), **prepare** at `timeToTurn ≤ 12 s` or `dist ≤ 200 m` (`buildPrepareCue`), **turn** at `timeToTurn ≤ 3 s` or `dist ≤ 40 m` (`buildTurnCue`); one cue per GPS tick via threshold crossing + catch-up (turn > prepare > ahead); continue-on-segment after step advance (distance kept); phrase text in `NavTtsPhrases.kt`
- Nav-start traffic TTS: after *"Starting navigation."* only on first `activateNavigationTracking()` — Tier 1 `TomTomTrafficClient.findJamOnRoute()` (120 m corridor, 10 km look-ahead, MODERATE+); Tier 2 `trafficDelaySeconds ≥ 120` from TomTom route or parallel TomTom fetch on OSRM pick; prefetched IO in `applyActiveRoute()` during route overview; skip if key blank, fetch fails, or prefetch not done; **not** spoken on reroute (`navStartTrafficEligible` gate)
- Voice navigation toggle: Map Settings **Voice navigation** (`LauncherPreferences.navigationVoiceEnabled`, key `navigation_voice_enabled`, default **true**); `CarMapEngine.setNavigationVoiceEnabled()`; TTS uses `USAGE_ASSISTANCE_NAVIGATION_GUIDANCE` + `AUDIOFOCUS_GAIN_TRANSIENT` (music pauses, not `MAY_DUCK`) — no bundled voice model
- Nav TTS volume: `LauncherPreferences.navigationVoiceVolume` (key `navigation_voice_volume`, default **1.0**, range **0.5-1.0** = Android `KEY_PARAM_VOLUME` ceiling) → `NavigationVoiceController.volume` via `KEY_PARAM_VOLUME`; optional **Boost guidance volume** boosts `STREAM_ACCESSIBILITY` + `STREAM_NOTIFICATION` to max while speaking; arrival TTS defers `startFreeDrive()` until utterance `onDone`; segment-aware maneuver phrases (`SEGMENT_TURN_ONLY_M` 60 m); reroute TTS min **30 s** apart; suppress maneuver cues when `isRerouteInProgress`

## TomTom routing

- `TomTomRoutingClient.kt` uses Calculate Route API (`traffic=true`, `routeType=fastest`) — requires Routing API on key, not just Traffic Flow; failures omit lighter-traffic alternate non-fatally
- ETA delta strings use **"vs conventional"** in `formatEtaDeltaMinutes()`
